114
00:07:58.231 --> 00:08:00.109
Core Concepts, Beginner to Deep.

115
00:08:01.359 --> 00:08:03.705
Intuition: a doctor's appointment book.

116
00:08:03.985 --> 00:08:06.396
A clinic doesn't cap appointments at 20 a day.

117
00:08:06.676 --> 00:08:14.505
A check-up takes 10 minutes and a procedure takes 45, so the receptionist books time, from the rota of the doctors on duty.

118
00:08:14.785 --> 00:08:17.815
Two receptionists must never give away the same time.

119
00:08:18.095 --> 00:08:22.212
The book is kept in pen, so who cancelled Tuesday at 3? has an answer.

120
00:08:22.492 --> 00:08:29.191
And when everyone wants Saturday morning, a good receptionist offers Friday evening first, before the patient walks out.

121
00:08:29.471 --> 00:08:33.311
Slot booking is that appointment book, for thousands of zones at once.

122
00:08:34.661 --> 00:08:35.621
Requirements.

123
00:08:35.901 --> 00:08:36.754
Functional.

124
00:08:37.034 --> 00:08:46.250
Generate slots per zone (for example, hourly or two-hourly, 7 days ahead) from templates, with cut-off times (book by Tminus 90 min).

125
00:08:46.530 --> 00:08:49.794
Show available slots for an address, with fees, quickly.

126
00:08:50.074 --> 00:08:56.111
Hold a slot during checkout; confirm on payment; expire abandoned holds (Ch 46).

127
00:08:56.391 --> 00:09:02.279
Cancel and reschedule; ops can change capacity (roster changes, rain) and close slots.

128
00:09:03.629 --> 00:09:07.448
Tell dispatch and stores what's booked (picking waves, rider plans).

129
00:09:07.728 --> 00:09:08.837
Non-functional.

130
00:09:09.117 --> 00:09:13.021
Slot listing p99 50 ms (it's on the checkout path).

131
00:09:13.301 --> 00:09:17.739
Never overbook beyond configured capacity, even at festival peaks.

132
00:09:18.019 --> 00:09:19.853
Full audit history of each slot.

133
00:09:20.133 --> 00:09:23.973
Availability shown may be seconds stale; booking must be exact.

134
