The row lock serialises bookings on a hot slot, and a failed condition is an immediate, clean full.

249
00:14:42.965 --> 00:14:49.088
SERIALIZABLE is correct without rewriting the logic, but pays in aborts on exactly the hot rows.

250
00:14:50.438 --> 00:14:56.113
Optimistic version append (event sourcing): the unique key is the guard; conflicts retry.

251
00:14:56.393 --> 00:15:00.233
Retries rise with contention, but you get the history (L3).

252
00:15:00.513 --> 00:15:10.838
Very hot slots: split capacity into sub-buckets (Ch 46 L1), or put a Redis gate in front for admission with the database as the source of truth.

253
00:15:12.188 --> 00:15:14.407
Holds, confirmations and expiry.

254
00:15:14.687 --> 00:15:16.863
A customer picks a slot before paying.

255
00:15:17.143 --> 00:15:21.729
The slot service holds the minutes (HELD), and payment success confirms it (BOOKED).

256
00:15:22.009 --> 00:15:33.252
Abandoned checkouts expire (HOLDEXPIRED) after a TTL, with the lease pattern from Ch 46 L2: short TTL, extended when payment actually starts.

257
00:15:33.532 --> 00:15:39.783
Late payment after expiry either re-books if there's still room, or triggers a refund and apology flow.

258
00:15:40.063 --> 00:15:44.692
Holds count against capacity; the listing shows cap minus held minus booked.

259
00:15:46.042 --> 00:15:47.877
The event-sourced slot aggregate.

260
00:15:48.157 --> 00:15:55.090
Ch 15 promised an event-sourced aggregate per slot, for contention plus an audit of who took which slot.

261
00:15:55.370 --> 00:15:56.330
The design:

262
00:15:56.610 --> 00:16:02.605
Event store: slotev(slotid, version, type, customer, minutes, at), PRIMARY KEY (slotid, version).

263
00:16:02.885 --> 00:16:08.751
Commands load the aggregate, validate (capacity, cut-off), and append with version + 1.

264
00:16:09.031 --> 00:16:13.106
A duplicate key means someone else won the race: reload and retry.

265
00:16:13.386 --> 00:16:18.911
Read model (projection): slotview(slotid, cap, held, booked) feeds listings (via cache).

266
00:16:19.191 --> 00:16:22.285
Projectors consume events via the outbox or Kafka.

267
00:16:22.565 --> 00:16:26.319
Snapshots every N events bound the load cost for busy slots.

