00:26:55.472 --> 00:26:57.989
Capacity (ADR-340).

427
00:26:58.269 --> 00:27:01.192
The roster service emits CAPACITYCHANGED events.

428
00:27:01.472 --> 00:27:06.805
The ETA service gives order cost per slot, with traffic by hour and door time by building.

429
00:27:08.155 --> 00:27:10.886
Concurrency (ADR-341).

430
00:27:11.166 --> 00:27:15.689
Hot slots see retries (L2: ~1 per 12 attempts overall).

431
00:27:15.969 --> 00:27:21.110
Retries are bounded, and past 5 of them we return try another slot with alternatives.

432
00:27:21.390 --> 00:27:25.721
A Redis admission gate is available as a flag for festival openings.

433
00:27:26.001 --> 00:27:28.518
Snapshots (ADR-342).

434
00:27:28.798 --> 00:27:32.531
Written asynchronously by the projector, never on the booking path.

435
00:27:32.811 --> 00:27:35.265
Holds (ADR-343).

436
00:27:35.545 --> 00:27:40.046
Expiry is a scheduled command that appends HOLDEXPIRED idempotently.

437
00:27:40.326 --> 00:27:42.886
Demand (ADR-345).

438
00:27:43.166 --> 00:27:47.667
Fee changes need Finance approval, and are tested by switchback per zone.

439
00:27:49.017 --> 00:27:50.041
Consequences.

440
00:27:50.321 --> 00:28:01.372
We take on more infrastructure (event store, projector, snapshots), eventual consistency in listings, dependence on the ETA estimator's quality, and event schema governance.

441
00:28:01.652 --> 00:28:08.777
In return we get honest slots, zero overbooking, auditable history, recoverable read models, and a demand lever.

