490
00:33:05.953 --> 00:33:06.870
On screen:

491
00:33:07.150 --> 00:33:24.003
60 slots times 840 rider-minutes; 32 workers; 12,000 booking attempts (70% want 8 hot. slots); real PostgreSQL. booking method booked slots over retries attempts per second p99. capacity.

492
00:33:24.283 --> 00:33:34.801
B1) read, check in Java, write back (READ COMMITTED) 2,965 60 0 4,880 31.6 ms.

493
00:33:35.081 --> 00:33:46.899
B2) same, SERIALIZABLE + retry 1,996 0 1,043 5,247 36.7 ms.

494
00:33:47.179 --> 00:33:49.121
B3) conditional UPDATE...

495
00:33:49.401 --> 00:33:58.489
WHERE used + m = cap 1,999 0 0 7,679 20.6 ms.

496
00:33:58.769 --> 00:34:17.926
B4) event-sourced append, PK(slot, version) + retry 1,998 0 1,020 5,192 35.4 ms. then B1 is the classic check-then-act race: two workers read the same 'used', both see. room, both book.

497
00:34:18.206 --> 00:34:23.987
SERIALIZABLE. detects it but pays in aborted transactions on exactly the hot slots.

498
00:34:24.267 --> 00:34:24.886
A.

499
00:34:25.166 --> 00:34:26.681
