00:37:22.437 --> 00:37:23.952
The rest is in the chapter.

521
00:37:26.802 --> 00:37:27.655
Reading it:

522
00:37:27.935 --> 00:37:32.501
A projector that forgets one event type corrupted 2,088 slots.

523
00:37:32.781 --> 00:37:36.898
442 of them turned customers away while they had room.

524
00:37:37.178 --> 00:37:43.023
Replaying the history (about 1 second for 819k events) repaired every one.

525
00:37:43.303 --> 00:37:45.906
A counter-only design would have no way back.

526
00:37:46.186 --> 00:37:48.021
Snapshots matter for hot slots:

527
00:37:48.301 --> 00:37:53.975
52 rows instead of 2,802, about 12x faster at p50.

528
00:37:54.255 --> 00:37:55.962
Quiet slots barely notice.

529
00:37:56.242 --> 00:38:01.405
Time travel and audit are ordinary SQL over the events: a few milliseconds each.

530
00:38:02.755 --> 00:38:05.400
L4, Moving demand to where the riders are.

531
00:38:05.680 --> 00:38:06.619
Requirement:

532
00:38:06.899 --> 00:38:09.907
Lose fewer customers without hiring more riders.

533
00:38:10.187 --> 00:38:12.853
The same zone, with capacity in rider-minutes.

534
00:38:13.133 --> 00:38:17.912
What the customer is shown, what they pay, and where the riders are rostered all vary.

535
00:38:18.192 --> 00:38:22.565
Customer acceptance and price response are stated assumptions (VERIFY).

